payload.explanation_en:
The correct answer is ```
int h = s.length() / 2;
return s.substring(h) + s.substring(0, h);
```. The second half starts at index h, so s.substring(h) + s.substring(0, h) swaps the halves exactly.
```
int h = s.length() / 2;
return s.substring(0, h) + s.substring(h);
``` is incorrect: Rebuilds the original string without swapping the halves.
```
int h = s.length() / 2;
return s.substring(h) + s.substring(0, h - 1);
``` is incorrect: Drops the last character of the first half.
```
int h = s.length() / 2;
return s.substring(h + 1) + s.substring(0, h);
``` is incorrect: Drops the first character of the second half.

