```java
class Steps {
    /** Returns the number of steps needed to reach 1 from n, where n >= 1. In each step, an even value is divided by 2 and an odd value greater than 1 becomes 3 * value + 1. */
    public static int steps(int n) {
        int count = 0;
        /* missing code */
        return count;
    }
}
```

payload.explanation_en:
The correct answer is ```
while (n != 1) {
    if (n % 2 == 0) {
        n = n / 2;
    } else {
        n = 3 * n + 1;
    }
    count++;
}
```. The loop runs until n reaches 1, applying the even or odd rule and counting once per step.
```
while (n > 2) {
    if (n % 2 == 0) {
        n = n / 2;
    } else {
        n = 3 * n + 1;
    }
    count++;
}
``` is incorrect: Stops when the value is 2 or less, so it misses the final step.
```
while (n != 1) {
    if (n % 2 == 0) {
        n = n / 2;
    } else {
        n = 3 * n + 1;
    }
}
count = 1;
``` is incorrect: Never increments count inside the loop.
```
while (n != 1) {
    if (n % 2 == 0) {
        n = n / 2;
    } else {
        n = (3 * n + 1) / 2;
    }
    count++;
}
``` is incorrect: Combines the odd update and the next halving into one step, so it counts fewer steps.

